# cron/crontab — times are Europe/Rome (ENV TZ in cron/Dockerfile). Spec §10.2.
# No --retry: a failed tick is retried by the next schedule, not by curl — jobs must run at most
# once per tick (src/platform/jobs/tick.ts records each job's own outcome before moving on).
# integrations-sync (docs/scheduler.md): each connection at the minute its owner chose. The minute
# tick runs only that job, and only when a connection is due; what reads the movements follows the
# sync. The hourly tick runs what goes by the date or by a stuck document, not by the movements.
* * * * *  curl -fsS --max-time 600 -H "X-Cron-Secret: ${CRON_SECRET}" -X POST "http://ledgerly:3000/api/jobs/tick?tier=minute"
30 * * * * curl -fsS --max-time 600 -H "X-Cron-Secret: ${CRON_SECRET}" -X POST "http://ledgerly:3000/api/jobs/tick?tier=hourly"
0 12 * * * curl -fsS --max-time 600 -H "X-Cron-Secret: ${CRON_SECRET}" -X POST "http://ledgerly:3000/api/jobs/tick?tier=daily"
5 0 1 * *  curl -fsS --max-time 600 -H "X-Cron-Secret: ${CRON_SECRET}" -X POST "http://ledgerly:3000/api/jobs/tick?tier=monthly"
